{"name":"Drops of God","hex":"#571e2f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"drops","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of drop"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of drop"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drops"},{"term":"god","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Godié."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deity or supreme being; a supernatural, typically immortal, being with superior powers, to which personhood is attributed.","An idol.\nA representation of a deity, especially a statue or statuette.\n Something or someone particularly revered, worshipped, idealized, admired and/or followed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/god"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drops of God","blocks":[{"text":"Drops of God  is a Japanese manga series written by Tadashi Agi, a pseudonym employed by creative team of sister and brother Yuko and Shin Kibayashi, and illustrated by Shu Okimoto. The story, about wine, is told in two parts – the first part focusing on protagonist Shizuku Kanzaki and his rival Issei Tomine on their search of the \"Twelve Apostles\" wines, and the second focusing on finding the \"Drops of God\". A third part of the series, serving as a short sequel, details Shizuku's life after the competition and taking Issei's daughter under his wing."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e8/Kami_no_Shizuku_JAPANESE_MANGA_VOL_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drops_of_God","wikidata":"Q706714"},{"title":"Drops of God (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Drops of God is a French-American-Japanese drama television series created by Quoc Dang Tran, directed by Oded Ruskin and starring Fleur Geffrier and Tomohisa Yamashita. It is based on the manga series of the same name written by Tadashi Agi and illustrated by Shu Okimoto. The series centres on the competition for inheritance of an estate and its vast wine collection between an heiress and a star student of a well-known oenologist who died. However, the former experiences severe side effects related to her childhood trauma and the latter's family complicates the process."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Drops_of_God_TV_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drops_of_God_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q111210240"},{"title":"God","blocks":[{"text":"A supreme deity, supreme being, supreme god, or simply just God, is a deity within theistic belief systems which is believed to be the ultimate cause of all things in existence. As such, it is seen as the creator, sustainer, and ruler of the universe. God is often thought of as incorporeal and independent of the material creation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Michelangelo%2C_Creation_of_Adam_04.jpg/330px-Michelangelo%2C_Creation_of_Adam_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/God","wikidata":"Q190"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Istanbul%2C_Hagia_Sophia%2C_Allah.jpg/500px-Istanbul%2C_Hagia_Sophia%2C_Allah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Istanbul%2C_Hagia_Sophia%2C_Allah.jpg/500px-Istanbul%2C_Hagia_Sophia%2C_Allah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIstanbul%2C_Hagia_Sophia%2C_Allah.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Tetragrammaton_Sefardi.jpg/500px-Tetragrammaton_Sefardi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t